SM(560,{"n":"2 Corinthians 4","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/2 Corinthians 4.mp3","d":2442.9,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study holy scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.96,"Okay, we'll go ahead and uh get started."],[23.28,"When we get started, we'll be picking up in uh St."],[26.0,"Paul's uh second epistle to the Corinthians uh at the beginning of chapter four, where we left off last time."],[35.04,"And so by way of brief review uh slash catch up, we're not that far into the epistle."],[44.16,"Uh we talked about how this is actually uh at least St."],[48.48,"Paul's fourth epistle to the Corinthians in actuality, uh, because there was a letter before First Corinthians, and there was at least a letter in between 1st and 2nd Corinthians. that we no longer have"],[62.2,"And we talked about how St."],[64.76,"Paul's visit uh between 1st and 2nd Corinthians uh did not go well."],[71.08,"Uh and um that uh he wrote uh that letter in between that we know about um in some sadness uh after how things had gone."],[85.8,"And we've seen that so far uh in the first three chapters, especially chapter uh chapter two, um, Saint Paul is really working with this letter to try and bring about some reconciliation uh between the people uh in the community."],[104.08,"And he's already sort of said on his behalf that he's forgiven everyone and has nothing against anyone."],[111.28,"He's been urging them to forgive each other, including some of the people who had to be kind of placed under discipline because of the way they were living."],[119.76,"There's some people who kind of, when he visited and when he was working to resolve these things, sort of came out on the wrong side of it."],[127.68,"And that resulted in some discipline."],[130.32,"But now he's urging them to bring them back and restore them, forgive them."],[136.92,"And we read in chapter three, Saint Paul went on to talk about the difference between the new covenant in which they were living and the old covenant, and about the glory of the Lord, about participating in what God is doing in the world, of looking upon the glory of God, and that their reconciliation is a part of what God is doing in the world."],[169.72,"And so that reconciliation will be transformative to them and then allow them to continue with what God is doing in their community in Corinth and in the whole the whole world through Christian communities like theirs."],[186.24,"So now we are picking up at the beginning of chapter four, unless there are any other lingering questions or comments or clues or hints left over from last time."],[202.88,"We'll go ahead and pick up in chapter 4, verse 1."],[208.4,"Therefore, since we have this ministry, as we have received mercy, we do not lose heart."],[214.72,"Now I mentioned before when we were reading Romans and when we were reading 1 Corinthians that when you see St."],[220.72,"Paul use the word therefore, that that marks an important transition in his argument."],[227.94,"Or in his uh the structure of his letter."],[231.3,"So he will sort of outline some theology."],[235.6,"Or some doctrine, some teaching, like we saw last time about the old and new covenants."],[238.96,"and And then he will say, therefore, he will sort of then apply what he's just been talking about."],[240.12,"He talked about Moses."],[247.69,"So I've taught you this."],[249.13,"Here's what this means now."],[251.03,"So here's what we're gonna do."],[254.95,"Um it is um usually yeah, no, usually it's un."],[262.47,"Um, sometimes there's some other constructions."],[266.87,"The un. Yeah."],[270.79,"It's uh sometimes he'll string a couple of particles together."],[275.35,"But it's it's that kind of transition."],[279.03,"Um sometimes it's uh oh poo."],[286.19,"Anyway. So um so he says, since we have this ministry, the ministry he was just referring to."],[295.64,"Um in terms of uh the the sort of unveiling of the glory of God."],[302.66,"And of reconciliation."],[306.02,"Okay. Um the ministry of the spirit, but that's what he's been saying."],[312.07,"Um since we've received this, we have this, we've received mercy."],[318.16,"Which is part of what that means."],[321.28,"We do not lose heart."],[323.44,"So he's saying we don't we don't lose heart despite all of this stuff."],[328.3,"Everything the community's been going through, everything I've gone through with you."],[333.34,"St. Paul has also talked about some of the things he went through on his own since he saw them last."],[338.44,"Despite all these things, we don't lose heart."],[341.34,"Because we've received mercy, from God."],[345.6,"And part of that mercy is this ministry, participating in what God is doing, is doing in the world."],[355.24,"But we have renounced the hidden things of shame, not walking in craftiness nor handling the word of God deceitfully, but by manifestation of the truth, commending ourselves to every man's conscience in the sight of God."],[370.6,"So this is a point that St."],[373.4,"Paul already made in 1 Corinthians in a different way when he talked about the life he lived among them."],[379.17,"But he's saying, you know, if you've been watching me, and all my dealers with you, there hasn't been any treachery."],[385.77,"He hasn't been saying they're scheming."],[388.55,"He hasn't been making crafty arguments with the scriptures."],[392.65,"Or about Christ."],[394.01,"He hasn't been playing games with them or trying to manipulate them and get them to do what he wants."],[399.73,"Um, and that wouldn't necessarily, I mean, some of these are like the hidden things of shame, obviously, would be a question of integrity."],[406.47,"I didn't say one thing to you, and then off in private, I lived a different way."],[410.44,"But in terms of the craftiness and and deceivelessness and stuff, um one could for for good reason, or with good motives at least."],[421.67,"Sort of scheme and plot and sort of manipulate people to get them to do what you want, saying, I'm trying to get you to do the right thing."],[429.52,"It's very common for parents with their children."],[431.97,"Like you just, you know, uh you're not you're not straight out lying to them, but you know, you're you're getting them to do what you want them to do, and you know, it's the right thing that they need to be doing."],[445.79,"Um, but St."],[448.35,"Paul's saying, I've I've never done that with you."],[451.89,"Because he says, part of that ministry, which he's just been describing, the whole issue with the veil and the glory of God"],[457.27,"He's his ministry is to manifest the truth to them, meaning to show it to them."],[462.96,"I think the truth of Christ, and I'm showing it to you."],[467.36,"And so he's saying that how he has operated is in keeping with what he just said, that hence the therefore."],[474.5,"If what they need to do is look into the glory of God and see what he's doing in the world, even if they don't like it, even if it scares them."],[483.0,"Even if it right, you can't veil it and hide it like they did in the old covenant."],[488.3,"Because remember, the people of Israel couldn't bear to see the glory shining from Moses' face, so he hid it."],[493.44,"And he's saying, We can't do that."],[495.36,"We have to look straight into it"],[497.85,"Then he has to, as a minister, show it to them."],[502.81,"He can't hide it from them."],[504.41,"He can't show them little pieces of it."],[507.34,"He can't sort of look at it himself and then just sort of get them to do what they need to do."],[513.84,"He has to show it to them if he expects them to see it and look at it, full on."],[524.26,"No. No. But uh mystery religions are."],[528.74,"Sure. Yeah, big light."],[530.5,"Yeah. So there are Roman, there are Roman mystery cults, there are groups that have secret rites and secret rituals."],[538.58,"And he says he has a clear conscience"],[539.44,"Behind the scenes."],[540.48,"St. Paul's saying no, he manifests it openly."],[545.44,"He finishes the verse saying he has a clear conscience about that before God."],[549.21,"That everyone has seen this is what he does, and this is how he lives."],[558.25,"Verse 3, but even if our gospel is veiled, it is veiled to those who are perishing, whose minds the God of this age has blinded, who do not believe lest the light of the gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God, should shine on them."],[575.53,"So he says, he's just said he isn't putting any veil in front of the gospel."],[580.77,"Remember, the gospel is the storyy, the account of what Christ has done, the victor he's won."],[582.13,"He's not veiling that"],[587.29,"He's not hiding any of it, any part of it."],[589.95,"He's fully. He says if it's veiled, if people can't see it."],[593.49,"If people aren't looking at it, if people aren't beholding and understanding it, that's not because of something St."],[600.05,"Paul's doing. That's because their own minds have been blinded."],[605.54,"Okay. So we'll start there."],[607.86,"That's kind of a long complex sentence."],[611.46,"So we'll start with their minds have been blinded, which sounds like a weird, it sounds a little weird in modern English because of the way we tend to think of the mind."],[622.34,"Okay. When we hear mind, we think of our brain."],[628.54,"As modern people."],[630.06,"And we think of our brain as being sort of like a computer."],[633.92,"It sort of processes information."],[635.68,"We take in information through our senses, brain processes it, spits out thoughts."],[642.88,"That's and that's how we that's how we think of it."],[646.4,"That is not at all how ancient people thought of the mind or what they meant by mind."],[652.0,"Okay. So the mind in Greek is is uh noose."],[656.64,"It's usually transliterated into English as N-O-U-S."],[660.32,"Okay And in the ancient understanding, there were a whole bunch of faculties of human beings. uh, that all fall under English words like mind and reason and that kind of thing"],[676.6,"They had it broken down a lot more."],[679.34,"So, for example, Aristotle distinguishes between five different intellectual virtues and properties."],[687.26,"One of which is the noose that we're going to be talking about more, the mind."],[691.2,"Here it's Dionia, but it's a cognate of the same word."],[695.52,"Um, but the other ones were wisdom, uh techni, which which is exactly what it sounds like."],[705.52,"It's where we get technology."],[706.8,"It's like know how."],[708.42,"Knowing how to do things."],[709.71,"If you're wrenching on your car, that's right."],[712.51,"That's your um right wisdom which is about like the book of proverbs right the understanding the world and moral situation uh phronesis which is uh moral reasoning knowing the right thing to do right in like a uh a uh moral uh in a uh an ethical an ethical situation and epistemia which is usually is similar similar enough to what we call science."],[746.51,"It's generally translated into Latin as scantia, so you know, where we actually get the word science."],[752.99,"And that's and that's like uh mathematical knowledge, would fall into that category."],[760.41,"Um, and that's a broad ancient understanding of mathematics that includes things like geometry and things that we would call science."],[769.13,"So those are all separate faculties for them."],[773.87,"We think about thinking and reason, and we lump all of that together, but they're really different if you think about them for even a minute, and there are plenty of people who have one or two of those and not all of them."],[787.39,"In fact, there's very few people who have all of them."],[789.81,"Even of the four I just defined."],[791.91,"There's lots of people who have one or two of them that they're really good, and then other ones maybe not so much."],[798.11,"Um so the the one on top of that."],[802.41,"The highest form of that is the one that's described as the noose that we translate as mind."],[809.82,"And so for for ancient people, the news, that capacity of the mind, is more like a sensory organ than like a computer that turns out thoughts."],[823.98,"We think of thoughts as being generated in our brain, and we think like the voice in our head, like our inner monologue, we think that's us."],[833.1,"Ancient people did not think that was them."],[837.66,"Okay, for for ancient people, thoughts come into your head from outside, and this is really. important not just for understanding the Bible, but for understanding the church fathers, because they talk the same way"],[850.5,"When they talk start talking about thoughts and that kind of thing, they're not talking about things that you generate yourself."],[858.92,"Thoughts come into your head."],[860.78,"Thoughts come into your mind."],[862.54,"Your mind sees them and apprehends them."],[864.54,"They come from outside."],[866.22,"And so ancient people believe those came from the spiritual world."],[872.7,"The spiritual world they refer to as noetic, which is from the same root as noose."],[879.26,"It's the world of the mind."],[881.19,"The invisible creation."],[884.21,"The unseen world."],[885.97,"That's all the world of the mind for them."],[890.89,"And so and this is this is not just for, I'm not just talking about like ancient Jewish people."],[898.49,"This is the whole ancient world."],[900.89,"So when Aristotle starts talking about God in his metaphysics, he believes he is ascending through his noose to see."],[913.71,"C in quotation marks."],[915.31,"I'm doing scare quotes for the recording."],[919.31,"The ground of being."],[920.77,"And and uh these uh numinal."],[924.63,"These uh invisible realities."],[928.15,"Okay. So this is the capa, this is the human capacity."],[931.35,"This is a place where a human being interfaces with the spiritual world okay is the the mind or the noose so that's what we're talking about here and so um thoughts come in from outside and this is why when you read the fathers and especially uh orthodox monastics talking about testing thoughts uprooting thoughts judging thoughts this is what underlies that the idea that you come to a place spiritually, particularly in prayer, where you're able to step back from that stream of thoughts that's always rushing through our heads from all over the place."],[973.99,"And step back and look at look at them and judge them."],[978.97,"And choose which ones are worthy and good, and which ones are bad and false, and remove those."],[984.75,"And so this is how the Jesus prayer works."],[987.33,"It's the prayer of a single thought."],[990.53,"So you pray it over and over and over again."],[993.09,"It focuses your instead of your mind being lost in a thousand thoughts rushing around past it."],[998.07,"And trying to keep track."],[999.52,"It's like looking at a busy highway."],[1001.3,"Now you're just focused on one thought."],[1005.08,"And then that's ultimately a way of working towards true contemplative prayer where you've got zero thoughts."],[1013.96,"And it's just you and and uh Christ."],[1018.17,"Um, but so that's the that's the the understanding of mind that St."],[1023.33,"Paul is talking about here."],[1024.85,"So when he talks about the blinding of their mind, blinding your brain doesn't make a lot of sense."],[1031.27,"So what they couldn't put two thoughts together."],[1033.28,"Like something stopping them from connecting the dots?"],[1036.8,"What No, it's that this capacity to correctly see the spiritual world, and to understand it and to see its terrain and the landmarks and to understand how to judge thoughts."],[1051.33,"That's been blinded."],[1053.15,"It's been darkened, so they can't see clearly."],[1056.99,"So even when the glory, of God, which is in Christ, as he said, specifically in the gospel of Jesus Christ, even when that light, the light of that glory is like shone right in their face."],[1070.1,"They're blinded, so they can't, they don't see it."],[1073.06,"It's shadowy. It's like it's like it's coming through a veil, even though there's no veil there."],[1079.06,"St. Paul hasn't put the veil there, but it's like there's a veil."],[1082.26,"Because they've sort of got this big cataract on their other spiritual eyes."],[1087.8,"That doesn't allow them to see it."],[1089.4,"I've seen the word noose translated as soul."],[1093.48,"Is that just wrong?"],[1095.24,"That's wrong, yeah."],[1096.12,"There's another word for soul."],[1099.16,"Yeah. Yeah. Siki is is the word for oh sure soul."],[1104.04,"Which usually it looks like psyche in yeah English yeah transliteration and nephesh in Hebrew so I mean like could that still be true today that I mean I've always thought that some thoughts could come from the outside like well no that is we is the Orthodox should we'd say that yes that is true."],[1122.0,"Okay that that is correct."],[1123.36,"Because I found that so and if if you think about it uh we don't experience generating thoughts we only experience the thought right we don't experience like writing them or coming up with them."],[1139.89,"Like they just appear."],[1141.37,"Yeah, yeah. Right spontaneously."],[1145.23,"Yeah. And then we acknowledge it one way or or another."],[1148.48,"So the mind is sort of this point of attention that we can direct at different things."],[1154.85,"Or let just diffuse across a thousand things."],[1160.95,"Yeah. And so, so uh St."],[1163.67,"Paul is saying, look, if there are people who aren't seeing, when I when I go and I proclaim the gospel."],[1170.57,"He says, I'm not veiling it, I'm not covering it, I'm not twisting it around, I'm not, you know, being clever with it, I'm just laying it out there."],[1178.57,"And if there are people who can't see it, it's because their vision is bad."],[1184.71,"Their spiritual vision is bad."],[1185.83,"He's had plenty of experience of finding that there are people like that"],[1190.07,"Yes. Well, he had that experience himself."],[1191.19,"To kind of get this across to him"],[1192.03,"Remember when he got knocked off the horse, he went blind."],[1197.27,"So he he had this taught to him in a very direct way by God."],[1201.83,"And then when he was baptized, the scales fell away from his eyes."],[1205.27,"So he's this is this is uh something he's had very a very literal form of experience with that he's talking about here."],[1216.47,"So their minds have been blinded by the god of this age."],[1221.51,"Okay. Little g."],[1223.83,"Little g, yeah."],[1224.87,"There's a reason why it's a little g."],[1226.55,"Yes. Yeah. Um, and that's that's talking about the devil."],[1231.37,"This age as opposed to the age to come."],[1235.83,"And I've talked before about this, but uh when we see the word God, even with a small g in the Bible, maybe especially with a small g, because we know when it has a small g, it's being applied to someone other than the God."],[1254.68,"Um we tend to get real nervous."],[1258.33,"Um and and that's because uh we've gotten very far removed as modern modern English speakers from the way the word God was used in Hebrew and Aramaic and Greek and in the ancient world."],[1275.69,"Um so uh I've talked before about the fact I know that in the probably several times that in in the Old Testament, uh the term God or gods is used for all kinds, it's used for basically the word Elohim."],[1290.38,"Yeah, which is like God, it's actually the plural of God, but is used to describe the god, pagan gods, uh dead the spirits of dead humans, uh in a few places like people's ancestors and stuff."],[1307.58,"Now, people didn't think their Aunt Martha was like the one who created the universe."],[1312.92,"Like no one thought that."],[1314.44,"Okay. So using that word to refer to Aunt Martha's spirit was not attributing that to her."],[1322.86,"The word just sort of meant a being who was a spirit."],[1327.04,"Who didn't have a body like ours."],[1329.97,"Um you'll find stuff from like Philo, who's Jewish, uh talks about how the sun, moon, and stars are gods."],[1343.17,"It doesn't have an issue with it."],[1345.93,"Because the just that word did not mean that."],[1351.82,"So the the other element, though, that I don't know that I've I've talked about in the context of this Bible study before, but that's important here, especially, is that when you say, like in this case, where we're saying the devil is the God of this age."],[1368.39,"Uh God, uh, and the fathers will talk about this sometimes."],[1372.87,"Uh, God is sort of a is more of a verbal concept than a nominal concept, meaning it's more of a verb than a noun."],[1384.52,"Uh in this, I'll give an example, uh, because we were just talking about monarchy before."],[1390.5,"King is very clearly a noun."],[1393.54,"Regent has a verbal concept."],[1398.75,"It's the person who's reigning."],[1401.49,"It's the person who's doing some function."],[1403.57,"Whereas a king is just that's what he is."],[1405.67,"It's a noun."],[1406.75,"God is more like regent."],[1411.36,"It's the one who's performing a function."],[1415.89,"So when St."],[1417.49,"Paul says, like he said in 1 Corinthians, there's many gods and many lords, but for us, there's one God."],[1426.97,"He's talking about there's only one being, in that case, the Father, who's filling that function."],[1436.38,"There's one who's filling that that function."],[1439.26,"Okay. So it's not by calling the devil the God of this age, it's not saying that the devil is a god' it's nots not saying the devil is god certainly right but it saying he's a god as if right there's like good gods and bad gods and and you know you know he's the he's he's the bad one who's fighting against the good one right it's not dualistic like that it's that the devil is the one who is filling that role in this present evil age that role is what the role of of ruler I would assume of of rule he's referred to as the prince of this world by Christ in in uh St."],[1482.92,"John's Gospel. It's interesting that he uses prince instead of king, also."],[1486.96,"But uh but also that I mean he's he's being worshipped in this age."],[1495.5,"Paul also said in First Corinthians, the sacrifices the Gentiles offer, they offer to demons."],[1509.72,"In some way or other, yes."],[1511.08,"He's talking about the pagans, yeah."],[1512.84,"So in this age, the person who but even even people who are Jewish and even maybe some people in the Christian communities are actually serving the devil, by their actions."],[1527.38,"By their actions."],[1530.24,"Um, so uh this this becomes important in talking to people today."],[1536.9,"Because most people today, um, very few people today, we'll put it that way."],[1543.38,"Very, very few people, even people who identify as pagans today, aren't sort of crass polytheists."],[1549.16,"The way we think about it."],[1550.97,"Um there aren't a lot of people walking around going around and saying, hey, I worship mammon or I worship Pluto."],[1561.35,"But there are plenty of people going around worshiping wealth and possessions."],[1568.47,"So when we say that's their god, we don't mean that there's like money sitting in the sky."],[1575.28,"That's like altar what it is."],[1576.8,"We mean that's who they're serving, and that's who they're worshiping, that's what they're sacrificing to in their life."],[1585.93,"So modern people are not that far removed from the Romans."],[1591.19,"The Romans worshiped the God of war, the God of beauty."],[1596.64,"The God of strength, the God of wealth."],[1601.49,"And so do modern people."],[1604.39,"In terms of what they're sacrificing themselves, their families, their children."],[1610.68,"Their life to, who and what they're serving."],[1614.17,"So, and ultimately, at at the the pinnacle of that triangle is the devil."],[1618.18,"Um, and so that that's what St"],[1623.71,"Paul means when he's when he calls the devil the God of this age."],[1629.09,"He's the one who the people out there outside of Christ's kingdom."],[1635.11,"Which he's working to extend."],[1637.08,"People outside of Christ's kingdom, that's who they're ultimately following when they chase after wealth and power and all of these things."],[1646.61,"None of them are gonna say, oh yeah, I worship the devil."],[1651.39,"But but ultimately, when you serve those other things, you're ultimately serving evil."],[1659.15,"Even if you're not aware of it at the time"],[1662.69,"And the problem with that, again, is not that these people are evil because they're doing that."],[1668.63,"The problem is doing that, going down that road is destroying these people."],[1674.85,"Destruction is at the end of that road."],[1678.45,"The devil's not going to treat you nice because you were a good worshiper."],[1683.33,"That's, you know, and and uh money and power and and beauty and all those things don't care about you at all."],[1690.38,"So it's the end is destruction."],[1692.88,"And so when when St."],[1694.64,"Paul is going out and trying to convert these people, again, it's not like Amway."],[1699.3,"And he's trying to get them to go and sell."],[1701.18,"Because that moves him up in the company"],[1704.9,"It's because he's trying to literally save them from the path that they're going down, from the course that they're following."],[1713.16,"To save them from the consequences of that."],[1716.44,"So that's that's who he means."],[1717.96,"He means the devil."],[1718.76,"That's why he calls him the God of this age or this world, depending on how it's how it's translated, this present age."],[1727.0,"Who has come and who is the one responsible for that blindness?"],[1732.81,"Is responsible for that blindness."],[1738.65,"And so they are not, do not believe less the light of the gospel of the glory of Christ."],[1744.97,"Because he doesn't want that"],[1746.18,"Who is the image of God should shine on them."],[1751.14,"The devil doesn't want that."],[1753.55,"That's important because I think I've read that in the past as God had condemned the."],[1762.27,"I'm an ex Calvinist, et cetera."],[1763.79,"Yes. Oh no, there are Calvinists who try to argue that this is God."],[1769.47,"It's all, I mean, everywhere else where you see the God of this world, the Prince of this world, in the New Testament, it's very clearly the devil."],[1776.51,"So arguing that this one isn't is kind of bizarro land."],[1780.91,"But there are Calvinists who want to argue that."],[1785.23,"That God has kept them from seeing them."],[1788.59,"Yes Because he doesn't want them to."],[1793.77,"I'm sure that there are um, I don't know if you could call them true Christians, but there are Christians like Orthodox Christians that are in the church, but are actually serving another master."],[1806.49,"Every time we sin, we're serving another master."],[1814.33,"Yes. This is the biblical picture."],[1817.76,"We look at we look at uh our actions from an ethical perspective."],[1824.24,"And what I mean by that is the modern British sense of ethics."],[1828.33,"Where it's I make choices, some external authority judges whether those choices were right or wrong, good or bad."],[1837.57,"That's not the way the scriptures look at our actions."],[1841.65,"The way the scriptures look at our actions is we are either participating in what God is doing in the world."],[1849.43,"And so we're bringing God's grace and his mercy and his love and his peace into the world through our actions by serving him."],[1858.55,"Or the exact opposite."],[1861.27,"We're bringing bringing the evil and sin and rebellion of the dark spiritual powers into the world."],[1869.51,"So the perspective, again to quote Bob Dylan, of the Bible is that you've got to serve somebody."],[1875.51,"You're never sort of just this free agent"],[1880.63,"It's one or the other."],[1882.55,"It's one or the other."],[1883.99,"And what you do, what you do brings those things into your world."],[1892.01,"Not the thoughts you think are the words you words you say, like some of the new age stuff."],[1895.94,"Oh, you need to speak positive things and then positive things will happen to you and all that nonsense."],[1899.86,"Not that. It's when you sin, you bring corruption and curse into your life and into the world."],[1905.46,"And we all know this because we've all had it happen, because we've all sinned."],[1909.8,"We've seen the pain and destruction and things that happen when we do."],[1913.78,"And hopefully, everybody here at least has seen at least a little bit that when we choose to follow Christ and we show love and forgiveness in these things, we've seen how that changes the world."],[1925.84,"Changes the world for us, changes our lives, changes our families, changes our life."],[1930.02,"Actual change happens based on what we do."],[1933.95,"Because we're bringing one or the other into the world."],[1939.07,"Into the world."],[1939.87,"And you have to understand that to understand almost anything in the Old Testament and most of the New Testament."],[1946.11,"I mean, all this stuff in the Old Testament about things being unclean and having to be purified and having to, that's because they were involved in sin."],[1952.59,"They were involved in wickedness."],[1955.33,"And that idea of purifying and cleaning and healing is all related to that idea that sin. does things to the world"],[1964.25,"And God's grace, on the other's positive side, does things."],[1970.09,"Does things to the real world."],[1975.21,"And we also should understand, related to that bizarro land Calvinist interpretation."],[1980.43,"That this isn't saying that the devil somehow picks some people and just stops them from being able to believe the gospel."],[1991.36,"Because this is why it's important that he he said doesn't say he blinds their eyes."],[1995.76,"He says he blinds their mind."],[1997.97,"Well, with the understanding of mind that we just talked about, what do you have to do in order? to do that"],[2005.69,"You just have to distract them."],[2010.42,"Because if your mind is a point of attention."],[2013.96,"And St. Paul's coming and trying to get you to look at, to look with it, to put your attention on Christ, who he is as he's revealed in the gospel, and what he did."],[2025.26,"And the devil comes along and puts into your head 23 pornographic images."],[2032.59,"Eight stupid song jingles uh worry about five things that are happening tomorrow, uh a pain in your toe and, you know, eight other things, that's all he has to do."],[2045.55,"That works just like a veil"],[2048.15,"Yeah. Because you're looking at all of those other things."],[2055.57,"It does mean such a common experience for me that when I'm trying to pray, I remember, oh I didn't do such and such that I ought to have done."],[2069.41,"Yeah, or hey, remember that stupid thing you said earlier?"],[2072.05,"Yeah. Is it that embarrassing?"],[2074.37,"Yeah. Yeah, or yeah."],[2080.37,"Because those thoughts are coming in from outside."],[2084.37,"So how is it that some people like like these people in this church that we're reading about?"],[2091.45,"How is it that they have gone or people today that they have that veil is going to lift to?"],[2095.53,"Like how does that happen?"],[2096.97,"Well, St. Paul says he's lifting the veil and preaching it to them, but what he's saying to them is that it's a question of this focus and distraction."],[2104.82,"This is why Christ talks so much, his ministry about worrying."],[2108.9,"You know, he's not just like, hey guys, your anxiety levels up here."],[2112.9,"If you want to live a successful and happy life, you need to bring it down."],[2117.8,"He's not a self help teacher."],[2121.37,"Worry, can lead you straight to destruction."],[2126.93,"It can wreck, it can wreck you."],[2129.42,"And so it it it it's a form of temptation."],[2133.8,"All of these things, distraction, these are all right forms of forms of temptation."],[2141.32,"So we we can find it in a way choosing the focus on what's being"],[2147.82,"And that this is this understanding is what underlies the whole practice of orthodox prayer, not just the Jesus prayer that I mentioned earlier, the prayer of a single thought, but the idea of having our prayer corner with icons, to focus our physical senses."],[2164.1,"And incense, and all of these things that help us focus and and narrow vision on one thing."],[2170.3,"This is why we start out reading written prayers."],[2174.11,"We have something in front of for. us to focus"],[2177.25,"And if you realize you've gone down half a page and have no idea what you read, you go back and start again."],[2184.69,"All these things are helps, our real physical aids to doing that."],[2190.07,"To try and get our attention focused for at least a moment on Christ without all the other all the other distractions."],[2201.59,"All the other distractions."],[2202.95,"That's the the temptations the devil gives us end up with things that are truly and obviously evil, but they don't start there."],[2211.29,"The devil doesn't just walk up to you one day and say, murder your whole family."],[2215.82,"Because that's that's not gonna work."],[2217.74,"It's not gonna work"],[2220.28,"He comes with those little things we were just talking about."],[2225.26,"And then it builds."],[2227.1,"More and more anxiety."],[2228.7,"More and more anxiety about money."],[2230.94,"What are you willing to do now to get money?"],[2234.8,"Or just what am I willing to do to escape from the stress."],[2241.14,"And the worry and the shame and the embarrassment."],[2244.18,"What am I willing to do?"],[2245.22,"Am I willing to go get drunk?"],[2246.5,"Am I willing to start using drugs?"],[2248.06,"Am I like, well, now I need drugs, and now I don't have money, and so now what am I willing to do to get money to get drugs or to get alcohol or to get this or to get"],[2254.79,"And it snowballs."],[2256.93,"Until we find ourselves in a place place. where we never would have gone deliberately in the first"],[2263.15,"We never would have in a million years chosen to live our life like that."],[2267.15,"But we end up there at the end of this long string of temptations."],[2270.91,"So it's just, it's just the next thought down the chain."],[2275.47,"And this is this is what the parable of the prodigal son illustrates so beautifully."],[2279.89,"If you'd come up to this son while he's living with dad in wealth and said, Hey, do you want to go live with pigs and eat their slop?"],[2288.59,"He wouldn't have said, sure, that sounds great."],[2291.07,"I'm out of here."],[2293.35,"That's not what gets said first."],[2295.83,"What gets said first is, man, how long are you gonna sit here and wait for your dad to croak so you can get some of that money?"],[2301.91,"Why don't you just ask him"],[2307.07,"He'll probably give it to you."],[2308.19,"Then you can go have fun."],[2310.27,"And then it was, well, this would be fun, and that would be fun."],[2313.8,"That's how it goes."],[2316.7,"And so St."],[2317.42,"Paul is saying, that's what has happened to these people."],[2322.08,"When we try to present the gospel to them, the devil has done all these other things."],[2328.77,"Christ talks about this in the parable of the sower, too."],[2331.66,"The birds, the devil comes and snatches it away."],[2335.23,"Or, you know, the we it starts to grow up, but then the weeds come."],[2339.81,"The cares of this world come and choke it out."],[2342.85,"Paul's talking about here"],[2345.35,"The same kind of idea that St."],[2348.93,"And so he's saying he makes it clear, he pulls back the veil."],[2352.53,"That's what they need to do too."],[2356.05,"When they're where proclaiming Christ's gospel, when they're seeking to show Christ to people, they have to constantly be pulling that veil back."],[2362.94,"And shining that light to try to get through all the haze and all the right everything else."],[2369.66,"They need to focus themselves and they need to try and broadcast it right 100% clearly to everyone around them."],[2376.62,"With no ambiguity."],[2377.1,"ambiguity And what would be the sources of?"],[2378.46,"Well, what did St"],[2381.91,"Paul just say about how he presented it?"],[2385.35,"The way he lives his life."],[2387.73,"If you're going and trying to talk about the gospel of Jesus Christ to your co-worker, and all he sees you do all day is complain and steal time from your boss, and right?"],[2399.51,"Or if you're if you could tell you're trying to manipulate him and trying to sell him on something."],[2404.61,"Or all these things St."],[2405.89,"Paul just said he doesn't do."],[2407.94,"They need to also not do."],[2409.46,"They need to have that integrity, as they're trying to perform this function, this ministry in their community."],[2420.46,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2427.58,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecouncil at ancientfaith.com"],[2433.22,"That's wholecouncil at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.96,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: reconciliation in Corinth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at <b>2 Cor 4:1</b>, where we left off</li><li class=\"d0\">Brief review: not far into the epistle</li><li class=\"d1\">this is at least Paul's <b>fourth</b> letter to Corinth</li><li class=\"d1\">one <b>before 1 Corinthians</b>, one <b>between 1st and 2nd</b> - both lost</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's visit between 1st and 2nd Corinthians <b>did not go well</b></li><li class=\"d1\">wrote the in-between letter <b>in sadness</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Chs 1-3, esp. ch 2: Paul working toward <b>reconciliation</b> in the community</li><li class=\"d1\">says he has <b>forgiven everyone</b>, nothing against anyone</li><li class=\"d1\">urges them to forgive each other</li><li class=\"d1\">some were <b>placed under discipline</b> for how they lived; had come out on the wrong side</li><li class=\"d1\">now: <b>bring them back, restore them</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Ch 3: <b>new covenant vs old</b>, the <b>glory of the Lord</b></li><li class=\"d1\">participating in what God is doing in the world; looking on God's glory</li><li class=\"d1\">their reconciliation = <b>part of what God is doing</b> → transformative, lets them carry on in Corinth and the world</li></ul>"},{"t":202.88,"lv":2,"h":"2 Corinthians 4:1 - \"Therefore... we do not lose heart\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:1</b>: \"Since we have this ministry, as we have received mercy, we do not lose heart\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Therefore\"</b> = marks an <b>important transition</b> (as in Romans, 1 Corinthians)</li><li class=\"d1\">he outlines theology/doctrine (last time: old vs new covenant, Moses)</li><li class=\"d1\">then \"therefore\" = <b>applies</b> it: \"I've taught you this, here's what this means now\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"This ministry\" = unveiling of God's glory, <b>reconciliation</b>, ministry of the Spirit</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Received mercy</b> → we don't lose heart</li><li class=\"d1\">despite everything the community has gone through, everything between Paul and them</li><li class=\"d1\">despite what Paul has gone through on his own since they saw him</li><li class=\"d1\">the mercy <b>includes the ministry</b>: participating in what God is doing in the world</li></ul>"},{"t":355.24,"lv":3,"h":"4:2 - No craftiness, manifesting the truth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:2</b>: \"renounced the hidden things of shame, not walking in craftiness nor handling the word of God deceitfully... commending ourselves to every man's conscience in the sight of God\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Same point as 1 Corinthians - the <b>life he lived among them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no treachery, no scheming</li><li class=\"d1\">no <b>crafty arguments</b> with Scripture or about Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">no games, no <b>manipulating</b> them into what he wants</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hidden things of shame</b> = question of <b>integrity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not one thing to their face and a different life in private</li><li class=\"d0\">Craftiness can have <b>good motives</b></li><li class=\"d1\">scheming/manipulating people toward \"the right thing\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"very common for <b>parents with their children</b>\" - not lying, but steering</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: <b>never did that</b> with you</li><li class=\"d0\">His ministry = <b>manifest the truth</b> = show it to them</li><li class=\"d1\">truth of Christ - \"I'm showing it to you\"</li><li class=\"d1\">fits the \"therefore\": look into God's glory even if it <b>scares</b> you</li><li class=\"d1\">old covenant: Israel couldn't bear Moses' face, so he <b>hid it</b> → \"we can't do that\"</li><li class=\"d1\">minister has to <b>show it all</b> - can't hide it, can't give little pieces, can't look at it himself and steer them</li><li class=\"d0\">Contrast: Roman <b>mystery cults</b> - secret rites, secret rituals</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: manifests it <b>openly</b>; <b>clear conscience</b> before God; everyone has seen how he lives</li></ul>"},{"t":558.25,"lv":2,"h":"4:3-4 - If the gospel is veiled","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:3-4</b>: \"even if our gospel is veiled, it is veiled to those who are perishing, whose minds the <b>god of this age</b> has blinded, lest the light of the gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the <b>image of God</b>, should shine on them\"</li><li class=\"d0\">He's just said he puts <b>no veil</b> in front of the gospel</li><li class=\"d1\">gospel = the story/account of what Christ has done, <b>the victory he's won</b></li><li class=\"d1\">hides no part of it</li><li class=\"d0\">If people can't see it, aren't beholding/understanding it → <b>not Paul's doing</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>their minds have been blinded</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Starting point: \"blinded minds\" sounds odd in modern English</li></ul>"},{"t":611.46,"lv":2,"h":"The ancient \"mind\" (nous)","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Modern: <b>mind = brain</b> = a <b>computer</b></li><li class=\"d1\">senses take in information → brain processes → spits out thoughts</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> how ancients thought of the mind</li><li class=\"d0\">Greek <b><i>nous</i></b> (N-O-U-S)</li><li class=\"d0\">Many <b>faculties</b> all lumped under our \"mind\" and \"reason\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Aristotle</b>: five intellectual virtues</li><li class=\"d1\"><b><i>sophia</i></b> = wisdom - Proverbs; understanding the world and moral situation</li><li class=\"d1\"><b><i>techne</i></b> = know-how; \"wrenching on your car\"; where we get <b>technology</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b><i>phronesis</i></b> = moral reasoning; knowing the right thing to do in an ethical situation</li><li class=\"d1\"><b><i>episteme</i></b> = science (Latin <b><i>scientia</i></b>); incl. math, geometry</li><li class=\"d1\">fifth = <b><i>nous</i></b></li><li class=\"d0\">We lump them; really <b>different</b> - few people have all four</li><li class=\"d1\">lots have one or two, strong in some, not others</li></ul>"},{"t":798.11,"lv":3,"h":"Nous as a sensory organ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b><i>Nous</i></b> = the <b>highest</b> of these faculties; what we translate \"mind\"</li><li class=\"d1\">here <b><i>dianoia</i></b>, a cognate</li><li class=\"d0\">For ancients: more like a <b>sensory organ</b> than a computer producing thoughts</li><li class=\"d0\">We think thoughts are generated in our brain - the <b>inner monologue</b> is \"us\"</li><li class=\"d1\">ancients: <b>not</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>thoughts come into your head from outside</b> - key for Bible <b>and church fathers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not things you generate yourself</li><li class=\"d0\">Mind sees and apprehends them; they come from the <b>spiritual world</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>noetic</b> world (same root) = world of the mind, <b>invisible creation</b>, unseen world</li><li class=\"d1\">whole ancient world, not just Jews: <b>Aristotle</b> ascends through his <i>nous</i> to \"see\" the <b>ground of being</b>, \"numinal\" invisible realities</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Nous</b> = where a human being <b>interfaces with the spiritual world</b></li></ul>"},{"t":931.35,"lv":3,"h":"Testing thoughts and the Jesus Prayer","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Why fathers/Orthodox monastics talk of <b>testing, uprooting, judging thoughts</b></li><li class=\"d1\">spiritually, esp. in prayer, you <b>step back</b> from the stream of thoughts rushing in from everywhere</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>look at them and judge</b> - keep the good, remove the false and bad</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Jesus Prayer</b> = prayer of a <b>single thought</b></li><li class=\"d1\">pray it over and over; instead of mind lost in a thousand thoughts - \"like looking at a busy highway\" - <b>one thought</b></li><li class=\"d1\">leads toward <b>contemplative prayer</b>: zero thoughts, just you and <b>Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So \"blinding the mind\" ≠ blinding the brain</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"couldn't put two thoughts together\" / failing to connect dots</li><li class=\"d1\">= capacity to <b>see the spiritual world</b> (terrain, landmarks, judging thoughts) <b>darkened</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Even when the <b>light of Christ's glory</b> shines in their face → shadowy, \"like coming through a veil\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul put no veil there; they have a <b>cataract on their spiritual eyes</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1089.4,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: nous vs soul; thoughts from outside","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: <b><i>Nous</i></b> translated as \"soul\"? A: <b>wrong</b> - another word</li><li class=\"d1\"><b><i>psyche</i></b> = soul; <b><i>nephesh</i></b> in Hebrew</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: can some thoughts come from outside <b>today</b>? A: <b>yes</b> - the Orthodox view, correct</li><li class=\"d1\">we don't experience <b>generating</b> thoughts - only the thought</li><li class=\"d1\">they just <b>appear spontaneously</b>; then we acknowledge them</li><li class=\"d1\">mind = <b>point of attention</b> - directed at things, or <b>diffused across a thousand things</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1160.95,"lv":3,"h":"Paul's own blindness and healing","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Paul: \"I'm not veiling, covering, twisting, being clever - just <b>laying it out</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">if people can't see it, <b>their spiritual vision is bad</b></li><li class=\"d0\">He had plenty of experience of people like that</li><li class=\"d1\">his own: <b>knocked off the horse, went blind</b></li><li class=\"d1\">taught <b>directly by God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">at <b>baptism the scales fell</b> from his eyes</li><li class=\"d1\">so a <b>very literal experience</b> behind what he's saying here</li></ul>"},{"t":1216.47,"lv":2,"h":"\"The god of this age\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Little g</b> - \"a reason why\" - = the <b>devil</b>; <b>this age</b> vs the <b>age to come</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Modern readers get <b>nervous</b> at \"god\" with small g</li><li class=\"d1\">far removed from how <b>Hebrew, Aramaic, Greek</b> used the word</li><li class=\"d0\">OT <b><i>Elohim</i></b> = actually plural; used for <b>pagan gods</b>, <b>spirits of dead humans</b> (ancestors)</li><li class=\"d1\">nobody thought \"<b>Aunt Martha</b>\" created the universe</li><li class=\"d1\">word just meant a <b>spirit being</b> without a body like ours</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Philo</b> (Jewish): sun, moon, stars are \"gods\" - no issue</li></ul>"},{"t":1351.82,"lv":3,"h":"\"God\" as a verb, not a noun","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Fathers: <b>God</b> is more <b>verbal</b> than <b>nominal</b> - function, not a thing</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>king</b> = noun, just what he is</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>regent</b> = verbal - the one <b>reigning</b>, performing a function</li><li class=\"d1\">God is \"more like <b>regent</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">1 Cor 8: \"many gods and many lords, but for us <b>one God</b>\" = only one being (the Father) <b>fills that function</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Calling the devil \"god of this age\" ≠ he <b>is</b> a god</li><li class=\"d1\">not <b>dualistic</b>: good gods and bad gods fighting</li><li class=\"d1\">he fills the <b>role of ruler</b> in this present evil age</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ in John: <b>prince of this world</b> (prince, not king)</li><li class=\"d0\">Also <b>worshipped</b> in this age</li><li class=\"d1\">1 Cor: sacrifices the Gentiles offer, they offer <b>to demons</b></li><li class=\"d1\">even some Jews, some in Christian communities, serve him <b>by their actions</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1530.24,"lv":2,"h":"Modern worship: wealth, beauty, power","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Today very few, even self-described pagans, are <b>crass polytheists</b></li><li class=\"d1\">nobody says \"I worship <b>Mammon</b> / Pluto\"</li><li class=\"d1\">but plenty <b>worship wealth and possessions</b> - not \"money sitting in the sky\"; = who you <b>serve and sacrifice to</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Romans: gods of <b>war, beauty, strength, wealth</b>; moderns the same</li><li class=\"d1\">sacrificing <b>selves, families, children, life</b></li><li class=\"d0\">At the <b>pinnacle of that triangle = the devil</b></li><li class=\"d1\">nobody says \"I worship the devil\"; serving those things = serving <b>evil</b>, even unaware</li><li class=\"d0\">Problem isn't that they're \"evil\" - that road <b>destroys</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">the devil won't treat you nice for being a good worshiper; money, power, beauty <b>don't care about you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">end = <b>destruction</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul converting people: <b>not Amway</b> (moving up the company) - literally <b>saving them</b> from the path and its consequences</li></ul>"},{"t":1753.55,"lv":3,"h":"Calvinist reading rejected","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: read this as <b>God</b> having condemned them? Speaker is an <b>ex-Calvinist</b></li><li class=\"d0\">A: yes, some <b>Calvinists</b> argue this is God keeping them from seeing</li><li class=\"d1\">everywhere else \"god/prince of this world\" = <b>clearly the devil</b></li><li class=\"d1\">arguing otherwise = \"<b>bizarro land</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>the devil</b> doesn't want them to see - \"he doesn't want that\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1793.77,"lv":2,"h":"You've got to serve somebody","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: Orthodox in the church but actually <b>serving another master</b>? A: <b>every time we sin</b>, we're serving another master</li><li class=\"d0\">Modern <b>British sense of ethics</b></li><li class=\"d1\">I make choices, an <b>external authority judges</b> right/wrong</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> how Scripture looks at actions</li><li class=\"d0\">Scripture: we're either <b>participating in what God is doing</b> - bringing his <b>grace, mercy, love, peace</b> into the world</li><li class=\"d1\">or the <b>opposite</b> - bringing the <b>evil, sin, rebellion</b> of dark spiritual powers</li><li class=\"d1\">\"to quote <b>Bob Dylan</b>, you've got to <b>serve somebody</b>\" - never a free agent</li><li class=\"d0\">What you <b>do</b> brings those into your world</li><li class=\"d1\">not the thoughts you think or words you speak - <b>not new age</b>: \"speak positive things and positive things happen\" - \"nonsense\"</li><li class=\"d1\">sin brings <b>corruption and curse</b> into your life and the world</li><li class=\"d1\">we've all seen the pain; and seen how <b>love and forgiveness change the world</b>, families, lives</li><li class=\"d0\">Key to the OT: things <b>unclean</b>, needing <b>purifying/healing</b> = tied to sin and wickedness</li><li class=\"d1\">sin <b>does things to the real world</b>; so does God's <b>grace</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1975.21,"lv":2,"h":"Blinding the mind = distraction","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not that the devil picks some people and <b>stops them believing</b> - that's the \"bizarro\" Calvinist reading</li><li class=\"d0\">He says the devil blinds the <b>mind</b>, not the eyes</li><li class=\"d1\">mind = <b>point of attention</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul urging you to put attention on <b>Christ</b>, the gospel, what he did</li><li class=\"d1\">devil's job: <b>distract</b> - \"23 pornographic images, 8 stupid song jingles, worry about 5 things tomorrow, a pain in your toe\"</li><li class=\"d1\">that works <b>just like a veil</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Common in <b>prayer</b>: \"I remember I didn't do such and such\" / \"remember that stupid thing you said earlier?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">thoughts coming in <b>from outside</b></li><li class=\"d0\">How is the veil lifted? Paul preaching it, but it's about <b>focus and distraction</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why Christ talks so much about <b>worrying</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a <b>self-help teacher</b> (\"bring anxiety down for a happy life\")</li><li class=\"d1\">worry can <b>lead to destruction</b> - a form of <b>temptation</b>; so are all distractions</li></ul>"},{"t":2147.82,"lv":2,"h":"Orthodox prayer as focus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">This understanding underlies <b>Orthodox prayer</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just the <b>Jesus Prayer</b> (single thought)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>prayer corner with icons</b> - focuses the physical senses</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>incense</b></li><li class=\"d1\">start with <b>written prayers</b> - something in front of you; if you're half a page down with no idea, <b>go back and start again</b></li><li class=\"d0\">All <b>physical aids</b> to get attention on Christ, if only for a moment, without the distractions</li></ul>"},{"t":2202.95,"lv":3,"h":"Temptation snowballs - the prodigal son","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Temptations end in truly, obviously evil things - but <b>don't start there</b></li><li class=\"d1\">devil doesn't say \"murder your whole family\"</li><li class=\"d1\">comes with the <b>little things</b>, then it <b>builds</b></li><li class=\"d1\">more anxiety about money → \"what am I <b>willing to do</b> now to get money?\" / to escape stress, worry, shame</li><li class=\"d1\">drunk → drugs → no money → what to get money for drugs? <b>Snowballs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">end up where you'd <b>never have gone deliberately</b> - \"the next thought down the chain\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Prodigal son</b>: wouldn't have said \"sure, live with <b>pigs</b> and eat slop\"</li><li class=\"d1\">first: \"how long are you gonna wait for <b>dad to croak</b>? just ask him\"</li><li class=\"d1\">then \"this would be fun, that would be fun\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: that's what's happened to these people</li></ul>"},{"t":2328.77,"lv":2,"h":"Pulling the veil back - integrity","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Parable of the sower</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>birds</b> = devil snatches it away</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>weeds</b> = cares of this world choke it</li><li class=\"d1\">same idea as Paul here</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul pulls back the veil; they must too</li><li class=\"d1\">proclaiming Christ, they must <b>constantly pull the veil back</b>, shine the light through the haze</li><li class=\"d1\">focus themselves and <b>broadcast 100% clearly</b>, <b>no ambiguity</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul just said how he presented it: <b>the way he lives his life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">witnessing to a <b>co-worker</b> while you complain and <b>steal time from your boss</b></li><li class=\"d1\">or he can tell you're <b>manipulating</b> him, selling him something</li><li class=\"d1\">all that Paul says he doesn't do → they must <b>not do</b> either</li><li class=\"d0\">Need that <b>integrity</b> to perform this ministry in their community</li></ul>"}]});
